    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1000">

                <pb facs="0873" n="757" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg757"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.113/249d.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the American Consul at
                        Chihuahua</hi>.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1000-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-24T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 24, 1912—7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The President’s proclamation of March 14 does not affect clothing, dry goods,
                    hardware, and foodstuffs, and Treasury Department has <pb facs="0874" n="758"
                        xml:id="pg758"/> issued orders to its officers on the Mexican border to
                    admit properly invoiced and manifested shipments.</p>
                <p>Exemption of dynamite for mines and other industrial purposes is still under
                    consideration by the Attorney General. Keep Department closely informed about
                    this.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1000-f1" n="2" type="source" xml:id="d1000-f1-content">
                <p>Same to consuls at Nogales, Ciudad Porfirio Diaz, Ciudad Juárez, Laredo, and
                    Ensenada.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
